"""Provider-independent policy text; safe to import in controlled-only paths."""
FLEXIBLE_POLICY=''' Also choose publish_artifact for general documents/checklists, self-describing structured-table/v1 data, or custom-view/v1 artifacts. Historical table/reconcile_csv is only the specialized invoice executor. Documents use title and stable block_id blocks, no kind; structured_table fields declare stable key,label,type,editable and explicit decimal scale/units or enum choices. Decimal cells are strings; row_id is stable; null means missing. Custom views contain bounded inert source {html,css,js}, readable fallback, current access_generation, exact bindable_artifacts references and declared read_binding actions with payload_schema {type:"object",properties:{},additionalProperties:false}. Source UTF-8 total <=48000 bytes, serialized body <=96000 bytes, bound bodies together <=48000 JSON bytes. Generated source runs only in the untrusted opaque-origin no-network frontend sandbox, never the backend. No fetch, credentials, provider, arbitrary target, save or approval action exists. Read actions return the exact saved document or structured table, not the latest replacement; revisions require a new binding. Preserve stable identities and human work; changes become proposals, never accepted. Artifact creation is useful draft work, not verification: do not assert execution, correctness or goal satisfaction. Use empty success_criteria for these drafts; only shape is checked. The existing sandbox bootstrap provides window.workagent.ready() (a promise resolving initial plain JSON, normally an empty object), window.workagent.data, and window.workagent.request(actionName, {}) (a promise resolving the broker response with binding, artifact_id, revision_id, body_hash and body). Wait for ready, call only a declared read_binding action, and render response.body. The host/broker validates the saved view and exact authorized data revision on every read. Keep exact artifact/revision/hash values in the declarative bindings, not embedded in source comparisons. In source, identify the declared binding by response.binding and validate the expected body shape; do not reject an otherwise valid host response because it differs from hard-coded artifact IDs, revision IDs or hashes. This lets an explicit human rebind reuse the same presentation without granting access to arbitrary data. Never substitute data yourself or retry against another target when a read is refused; structured table rows contain cells:[{field_key,value}], not a values object. Use local DOM controls for filtering, sorting or visualization; catch refused/stale reads and show a readable error without pretending fresh data was loaded. No fetch, imports, packages or external assets. DOM state is ephemeral; durable changes use trusted shell human-save/proposal controls.'''
